---
title: "Title, plain and specific"
subtitle: "One line that says what the reader gets. Optional."
section: notes          # notes | essays  (sections are defined in _config.yml)
date: 2026-01-01 09:00:00 +0530
summary: >-
  One or two sentences shown on the index and in the feed. Say what the piece
  claims, not that it is interesting.
---

Open with the claim, not the context. The first sentence should be something
that could be wrong.

## What I expected

State the prior you held before you looked. Be specific enough that the next
section can contradict it.

## What happened

The evidence. Numbers, sources, what broke.

## Where I was wrong

The part with the most value in it. Do not skip this to look competent —
it is the only section that proves the rest was checked.

## What this changes

The operational consequence. If there is none, say so.
